{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510337-accidental-deaths-of-werewolves","id":1510337,"title":"Accidental deaths of werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-01T01:56:38-07:00","id":1510337,"title":"Accidental deaths of werewolves","content":"I'm trying to set up a backstory for a Kinfolk campaign where a skinwalker has killed a bunch of garou and it's up to the remaining kinfolk to discover how it happened and I was wondering if a kinfolk wanted to kill a Homid werewolf and make it look like an accident, what means could they use to accomplish their goal? Obviously any sort of combat or combat-like situation is highly unlikely to work so no car-crashes, farm machinery accidents, or other heavy impacts.<br /> <br /> Could a werewolf be drowned? Gassed? Poisoned? I need it to be believable and with some useful detail as it's part of an investigation by the (non-professional) PCs.<br /> <br /> Similarly could a kinfolk somehow capture a werewolf and restrain them long enough to kill them? Disposal of the body is not an issue.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Bonus points if the body is left intact as the skinwalker needs the corpse for the ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 05-01-2023, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T04:18:30-07:00","id":1510344,"title":"","content":"In their breed form* the Garou don't have any special protections by default. They cannot soak lethal or aggravated damage and they are not resistant to things humans or not resistant to. Aim for the physically less fit ones (that would be on the lower spectrum of stamina) and make sure you take them out without them being able to react. So poisons, knocking them out and then doing things to them while they are unconscious, headshots from a safe distance while they are walking aound, making sure they fall into a woodchipper... They all work. The only problem is that if they get to react (if they last longer than one round), you're dead. However,as long as you make sure they don't get to react after your first approach, you're golden.<br /> <br /> Also, if you try poisoning or gassing them and they have Resist Toxin... well. Nice knowing you.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Metis are protected in all forms, they don't have the resitance to silver other forms do, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":".  Metis. 05-01-2023, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T07:54:36-07:00","id":1510358,"title":"","content":"Pretty much yeah, you effectively have to be killed in breed form before you have time to shift or are unable to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> WARNING BELLOW STATEMENT INVOLVES DISTURBING IRL STUFF.<br /> <br /> otherwise its going to be difficult their was an industrial accident in my gf home town where a man was trapped in an industrial oven where temperatures raised to around 280c for an extended period. That's probably around the level of damage its going to take to kill a garou by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-01-2023, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T08:39:13-07:00","id":1510364,"title":"","content":"As it has been said, a Garou is most vulnerable in the form they were born in, the problem is that since you need the body, even if the death is ruled an accident, it would be hard for some other Garou not to be looking around, unless the death was caused by falling off a cliff or during a mission, if he is lupus then illegal hunt is also an option, defeated when alone is also good if you attack a Silent Strider or BG that travel. That said, I think it would make more sense for you to blame someone else, like a wyrm creature, hunters, another of the changing breeds, another option would be attack Garou that no one cares about, Metis, Ronin or members that the tribes only tolerate. One question, do you intend to do this with just one kinfolk or do have several involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T08:48:11-07:00","id":1510366,"title":"","content":"Well, of course, close the doors of the Griffith Park Observatory on one... accidently ^^<br /> Okay, jokes aside, in WoD knowledge is the main weapon, not powers<br /> The primary role of Kinfolk to their Tribe is to be breeding stock and an individual Kinfolk's Renown (particularly within the Tribe) is greatly impacted by his or her fertility, Kinsman or Kinswoman's degree of Pure Breed also raised these odds, making the purity of tribal blood in a Kinfolk an important commodity and giving those more refined in the Tribes inherited features greater stock as it did with their true breed kin.<br /> Kinfolk held other roles and responsibilities within their Tribes, Septs, and the overall Garou Nation however. Childcare was of course an obvious role. Financing, politicking, and bureaucratic maneuvering on behalf of the Garou, directly or in their interests, made certain Kinfolk indispensable to their true-breed kin, spirit-warriors who Rage separated from humanity and its world. Since silver had no impairment to Kinfolk, certain rare individuals acted as Fetish-crafters, particularly klaives.<br /> Whatever their calling, Kinfolk were expected to care for and provide services for and to their true-breed relatives.<br /> ...and more often than not, Kinfolk are... not really treated fairly or good.<br /> Some still treat their kinfolk like &quot;mom&quot; and &quot;dad&quot; because that's what they are. On the other extreme they are glorified breeding stock<br /> There's a lot of variation, even among tribal members. Remember Rage kind of makes Garou assholes and failures at best, catastrophes at worst in &quot;human&quot; relationships.<br /> The spectrum is ranged between the &quot;we prize our kinfolk and celebrate them for who they are&quot; and scaling to &quot;breeding stock, but prized breeding stock&quot; (for Silver Fangs especially, Silver Fangs treat their kin like prize purebred stallions and mares, with prime bloodlines and higher percentage of Shifter offspring making kin become outright bargaining chips in political negotiations) to the &quot;Good night, I'll most likely kill you in the morning&quot; (Fenris and Furries) <br /> <b>Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes </b>and <b>Kinfolk: A Breed Apart</b> (K:UH W20 version besically) I highly suggest to read if you havent done it already, becasue it helps you to form a pciture of the Kinflok(s) in question relationships with the Tribe/Sept/etc and more importantly, their knowledge and resources<br /> When you armed with knowledge all you need is opportunity<br /> For example, Bone Gnawer kin comprise a fantastic network of casual spies. No one cares if the janitor or bum on the corner overhears a conversation or &quot;scouts&quot; a certain area... after the Garou trust his information, there is enoug one deathtrap and send the team in their death. Accidents happen. <br /> And if you are backed with the minions of the Wyrm? Skindancers you mentioned or just sensitive and spiritual enough to hear the whispers o the Spirits (in this case a Bane), or ended up in the business end of a vapire fangs and became addicted to the Kiss... the list is long, the opportunities are endless.<br /> The Kinflok have Lore and Knowledge and <b><i>the Garou don't expect a betrayal</i></b> from their Kin (even tho' treat them like dirt sometimes)<br /> So the pack is crashing at your apartman and not afraid to sleep? Quietly just slip their throats while sleeps in their breed form... simple and efficient. Quick and dirty.<br /> \u200bIf you want to kill them for their pelt and want them for a Skindancer ritual is harder, but if you just want them dead? <br /> Manipulate the circumstances, so they willingly rush in to their death and blame on their Rage or Hunger for Honor and Glory... or cry with the others while they are protomed posthumusly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T10:51:57-07:00","id":1510376,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's an edition thing but Garou can soak lethal in their breed form, at least in 20th. Like, homid is a weak form but the few dice it offers can save them from anything minor.<br /> <br /> Personally, an accident is unlikely especially if you're going to skin them. &quot;oh look he fell off a ladder and then his skin went missing&quot; doesn't cut it.<br /> <br /> it's more likely that you'd survive by<br /> A: killing the Garou and casting the blame elsewhere and then taking your long planned leave and saying goodbye before casting the ritual<br /> B: faking your own death alongside them.<br /> C: killing them in a place they'll never be found. Or at least attempt to: by some fluke or poor planning the bodies surfaced.<br /> <br /> really strong poison could work in large quantities. A lack of oxygen could deal with those pesky bone gnawers but needs a lot of setup. Ultimately, you want them in a scenario where they can't fight back. If you work with them on missions, you have chances to kill them all: blow up the factory, sabotage their parachutes, drive the boat away and shoot them from a distance. Truthfully, I think if you want to bag the whole pack at once, you'll need an accomplice: could be a relative, someone also with a grudge, and it could be someone you betray after. But someone to drive the vehicle while you shoot, or to lock down that second exit, or to flank them, is really handy. A nice open area, a vehicle, a rifle and a driver is one way to get them all at once. A fully-automatic weapon could wipe them out in a turn, though they're hard to get a hold of. Bombs are fun, get them in a tight space and blamo; Maybe the skinwalker's scars from the shrapnel will tell an interesting story.<br /> <br /> Gifts like Jam weapon/Tech are really good but a knowing kinfolk could get around them. The fact that X and Y were asking questions before the killings is always a great clue. Staying out of range or sniping the one with that gift first is a good measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:09:01-07:00","id":1510407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510337-accidental-deaths-of-werewolves?p=1510376#post1510376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's an edition thing but Garou can soak lethal in their breed form, at least in 20th. Like, homid is a weak form but the few dice it offers can save them from anything minor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wrong. Page 255 W20 clearly states:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"335\" height=\"114\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5MYiITp.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5MYiITp.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5MYiITp.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T17:26:47-07:00","id":1510442,"title":"","content":"Samuel Haight's Child of Gaia father was in fact decapitated in a car crash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T00:43:12-07:00","id":1510469,"title":"","content":"Also people often think you need furs for the rite. You don't. You need breed form skins. That means most of the victims will be skinned human skins as the most numerous Garou available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T03:30:03-07:00","id":1510478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510337-accidental-deaths-of-werewolves?p=1510407#post1510407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's wrong. Page 255 W20 clearly states:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"335\" height=\"114\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5MYiITp.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5MYiITp.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5MYiITp.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ok, I was reading 290<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lethal damage can be soaked by Garou and many other supernatural creatures at difficulty 6. Humans can-not normally soak lethal damage, although exceptionally tough ones may be able to try and soak it (Storyteller\u2019s option) at difficulty 8.\u2022 Aggravated damage, other than that inflicted by silver, can be soaked by Garou at difficulty 6 in any form except their breed form. Silver damage cannot be soaked in any form except the breed form, and metis Garou can\u2019t soak it at all. </div> </div> </div>Like, no distinction is made here for lethal, but a lot of distinction is made for aggravated, so you can see the implications. <br /> <br /> <br /> There are a fair few contradictions in WoD books so it makes sense to go with whatever interpretation you like more. For me, soaking lethal in breed form makes more sense; they have gifts and rage in breed form, and they have limited regenerative capacity (slow enough to be represented by fluff rather than rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T04:02:46-07:00","id":1510480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510337-accidental-deaths-of-werewolves?p=1510478#post1510478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a fair few contradictions in WoD books so it makes sense to go with whatever interpretation you like more. For me, soaking lethal in breed form makes more sense; they have gifts and rage in breed form, and they have limited regenerative capacity (slow enough to be represented by fluff rather than rules)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put this down to an editing error as the breed form limitation was always like that. The same page also says that aggravated wounds can only be healed by magic, even with the Garou healing one aggravated per day naturally.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}